/**
 * What Studio offers in its palette: your registered components.
 *
 * Generated by the Studio CLI, then reviewed:
 *
 *   csdx studio:component:register --component-dir=src/components/compound   (Session 1)
 *   csdx studio:component:register --component-dir=src/components/atoms      (Session 1)
 *   csdx studio:component:register --component-dir=src/components/layout     (Session 1)
 *
 * The CLI reads each component's TypeScript props and writes one entry per
 * component: a `type` (the id saved in every template, so never rename it), a
 * display name, and its props with a Studio type each. Lines marked `// added`
 * are what a developer adds after reading the generated file:
 *
 *   wrap: false   with `studioAttributes` spread on the component's root
 *                 element, so selecting it on the canvas selects it, not a
 *                 wrapper <div> Studio would otherwise add around it.
 *   sections      the palette group it appears in.
 *   thumbnailUrl  its preview in the Components panel (src/studio/thumbnails.ts).
 *   defaultValue  what a freshly dropped component shows before it's bound.
 *   design: true  (Session 2) the prop is set per breakpoint; see below.
 *   countProp     (Session 3) a slot whose children follow a number prop:
 *                 the Stack's Areas.
 */
